<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market slow, steady - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market slow, steady - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade slow. Few sales slaughter steers and heifers steady.</p>
<p>Inquiry moderate, demand fair.</p>
<p>Sales confirmed on 1,000 slaughter steers and 500 slaughter heifers Thursday.</p>
<p>For the week to date 107,300 head confirmed including 18,800 head or about 18 percent previously contracted or formulated cattle.</p>
<p>Slaughter steers: Select and Choice 2-3 1175-1335 lbs 64.00. Slaughter heifers: Select and Choice 2-3 1050-1200 lbs 64.00.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
